    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūpus</span></b> , i, m.
		root pu-, to beget; cf.: puer, pubes. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A boy</i>, <i>a child</i>, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 156, 22</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as a term of endearment,</span>”
				<i>puppet</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The pupil of the eye</i> (post-class. for pupula
			and pupilla), <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. Carm. 20,
			179</span></i>.</div>
